st: 3.905% at 6 mm (28% worse than F2 at 4 mm)\n- F3 best: 5.039% at 6 mm (65% worse than F2 at 4 mm)\n\n### Supporting Rationale:\n\n1. **Best Energy Resolution**: Absorber-F2 at 4 mm achieves the best possible energy resolution among all tested configurations\n2. **Material Properties**: F2 is described as \"dense alloy with a short radiation length\" which is optimal for electromagnetic calorimetry\n3. **Manufacturing**: All three materials can be machined to required tolerances (per candidate_specs.md)\n4. **Compatibility**: The mechanical support design is compatible with all candidates (per meeting_notes_2026-05-14.md)\n5. **Optimal Thickness**: 4 mm represents a sweet spot, balancing sampling frequency with shower development\n\n### **FINAL RECOMMENDATION**:\n\n**Material**: Absorber-F2  \n**Plate Thickness**: 4 mm  \n**Expected Energy Resolution**: 3.053% at 100 GeV\n\n**CAVEAT**: The dose rate constraint (\u226420 \u03bcSv/h at 1 m after 7 days cooldown) is a hard requirement that **has not been verified** due to lack of activation data in the available documentation. Before final approval, dose rate measurements or activation simulations must be performed for Absorber-F2 to ensure hands-on maintenance is possible.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LmooYsLfNdtg2BD6cEWvvs", "input": {"results": {"final_recommended_material_option": 2, "final_recommended_thickness_mm": 4, "final_expected_resolution_percent": 3.053, "all_requirements_verified": 0, "dose_rate_requirement_verified": 0, "material_requirement_satisfied": 1, "thickness_requirement_satisfied": 1, "resolution_optimized": 1, "improvement_over_F2_baseline_percent": 4.6, "improvement_over_F1_baseline_percent": 21.9, "improvement_over_F3_baseline_percent": 39.4, "verification_complete": 1}}, "name": "record_results", "type": "tool_use", "caller": {"type": "direct"}}]}
